<article class="helios-journal-story"><a href="{{ routes.root_url }}?view=journal-world-of-helios-1">← World of Helios</a><h1>RHODES ORIGIN: BEFORE EVERY IMPRINT IS A BEGINNING</h1><div class="helios-journal-story__body rte">
         

<div>Table of Contents 
  
</div>
<div></div>
<div><p>Ten years can be told through many milestones: collections, familiar symbols, opened stores, or silver pieces that have accompanied wearers for years. But looking back at HELIOS&#x27; journey, a more important question arises: before all of that, where did we begin?</p>
<p>The Rhodes Origin Helios Ring was created from that very question. Representing Chapter 1 - Origin in the 10-year journey, the ring doesn&#x27;t try to tell HELIOS&#x27; entire history on one piece of silver. It returns to a time when things were still incomplete, when the brand only had the first indications of the path it wanted to take.</p>
<h2>When everything started with a small promise</h2>
<p>Before collections, products recognized at a glance, or marks that have stayed with wearers for years, there were imperfect early days. There were rough sketches, incorrect attempts, stumbles, and choices that had to be redone. But it was during that time that one thing was established: if we were going to do something, it had to be good enough to be kept.</p>
<p>Rhodes Origin returns to that original spirit. Not to romanticize the past, but to remind us that behind every long journey is a very simple decision at the starting point: to begin and continue working until what you believe in becomes clearer.</p>
<p><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0644/2958/8701/files/rhodes-origin-truoc-moi-dau-an-deu-la-mot-khoi-dau-1.jpg?v=1787109505" alt="RHODES ORIGIN: TRƯỚC MỌI DẤU ẤN ĐỀU LÀ MỘT KHỞI ĐẦU - ảnh 1" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></p>
<h2>Rhodes - A starting point towards the sun</h2>
<p>The name Rhodes is inspired by the Greek sun island, a land associated with Helios - the sun god in Greek mythology. This is also a direct link to the name HELIOS itself and the inspiration that appeared from the brand&#x27;s early days.</p>
<p>The sun on Rhodes Origin therefore doesn&#x27;t just play a decorative role. It takes the ring back to an old layer of memory: the time when the name HELIOS, the first symbols, and the brand&#x27;s initial spirit began to take shape. If the sun symbolizes the starting point, then the remaining details on the ring tell the story of the journey taken since that starting point.</p>
<p>On the ring band are the name HELIOS, the sun, and lines that feel like scratches and the marks of time. Instead of making everything too perfect, Rhodes Origin retains the feeling of an object with a story. Because a journey of growth is rarely made up of pristine surfaces.</p>
<p><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0644/2958/8701/files/rhodes-origin-truoc-moi-dau-an-deu-la-mot-khoi-dau-2.jpg?v=1787109505" alt="RHODES ORIGIN: TRƯỚC MỌI DẤU ẤN ĐỀU LÀ MỘT KHỞI ĐẦU - ảnh 2" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></p>
<h2>Lotus - A symbol that accompanies change</h2>
<p>At the forefront of Rhodes Origin is the Lotus, one of the symbols associated with HELIOS through various stages. But the Lotus on this ring does not stand alone as a mere identifying detail. It is nestled among the signs of the past, just as a value can be preserved while everything else continues to change.</p>
<p>In ten years, products may change, and the way HELIOS tells its story may also evolve. But a brand does not grow by erasing everything that once existed. Some things need to be developed, some need to be re-examined, and some values need to be held tighter the further one goes.</p>
<p>The Lotus on Rhodes Origin thus becomes the connecting point between the beginning and the current HELIOS. It is not a symbol that frames the past, but a sign that some things continue to live on as the brand enters a new chapter.</p>
<p><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0644/2958/8701/files/rhodes-origin-truoc-moi-dau-an-deu-la-mot-khoi-dau-3.jpg?v=1787109505" alt="RHODES ORIGIN: TRƯỚC MỌI DẤU ẤN ĐỀU LÀ MỘT KHỞI ĐẦU - ảnh 3" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></p>
<h2>A signet ring for a personal mark</h2>
<p>Rhodes Origin is developed on the structure of a signet ring - a type of ring traditionally associated with seals, identity, and symbols representing the wearer. Historically, the face of a signet ring would be engraved with family crests, coats of arms, or personal symbols and used as a form of authentication: &quot;This is my mark.&quot;</p>
<p>HELIOS chose this structure for Chapter 1 because Rhodes Origin also embodies the spirit of a seal. On it are the signs of HELIOS&#x27; beginnings, but once the ring leaves the workbench, the brand&#x27;s story is only the initial part.</p>
<p>The rest belongs to the wearer.</p>
<p>New scratches will appear. The silver surface will change over time. The ring may accompany work, travels, ordinary days, or a milestone whose meaning only the owner understands. After a few years, two Rhodes Origin rings that started out identical may no longer be the same. These changes transform a piece of silver into a personal mark, because no two people travel the same journey.</p>
<p><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0644/2958/8701/files/rhodes-origin-truoc-moi-dau-an-deu-la-mot-khoi-dau-4.jpg?v=1787109505" alt="RHODES ORIGIN: TRƯỚC MỌI DẤU ẤN ĐỀU LÀ MỘT KHỞI ĐẦU - ảnh 4" loading="lazy" width="64" height="64"></p>
<h2>The first chapter of HELIOS&#x27; 10 years</h2>
<p>In its 10-year journey, Rhodes Origin is not a summary. It stands at the opposite end: Chapter 1.</p>
<p>Because before talking about the marks that have been created, HELIOS wants to return to where it all began. Not to relive the past, but to understand what brought the brand to the present. There are stages that need to be revisited not because they were perfect, but because those initial experiments, stumbles, and decisions laid the foundation for what came after.</p>
<p>Ten years is long enough to realize that a brand is not made by a single moment. It is made by many small decisions held long enough.</p>
<p>Before every mark is a beginning. A mark can only exist after someone has made the first stroke.</p>
<p>Rhodes Origin preserves that first stroke of HELIOS: the name, the sun, the Lotus, the imperfect traces, and the spirit of wanting to create something worth keeping. But the ring does not ask the wearer to live with HELIOS&#x27; story. It merely gives the wearer a starting point.</p>
<p>From there, each person will write their own continuation.</p>
<p>Perhaps after many years, the lines on the silver will no longer be the same as on the first day. Perhaps some scratches will appear exactly where it was once most polished. But like people, an item kept long enough will no longer be pristine in its original sense.</p>
<p>It gains memories.</p>
<p>Rhodes Origin - before every mark is a beginning.</p>
<p>And sometimes, the most important thing is not knowing where you will go from day one.</p>
<p>Just start. Then keep going.</p></div>
  

